<title>INDIA: Indian Jan 24-sector industrial output up 5.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Indian Jan 24-sector industrial output up 5.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's 24-sector industrial production index rose by 5.0 percent in January over the same month in 1996, the Industry Ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The index increased by 4.9 percent between April 1996 and January 1997 compared to the corresponding period in the previous year, the ministry said in a statement.  </p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>    24-SECTOR INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION	Jan 97    Apr96-Jan97</p>
<p>    Electricity				   +5.0	  +3.8</p>
<p>    Coal					    +2.5	  +5.8</p>
<p>    Saleable steel				+0.5	  +2.8</p>
<p>    Crude petroleum			     -9.2	  -8.8</p>
<p>    Petroleum Refinery Products	     +9.7	  +6.9</p>
<p>    Cement					  +7.2	  +9.8</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>    SIX INFRASTRUCTURE INDUSTRIES	   +2.9	  +3.3</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>    Steel ingots				  +2.0	  +3.1</p>
<p>    Nitrogenous fertiliser		    -4.2	  -3.2</p>
<p>    Phosphatic fertiliser		    +14.5	  +1.3</p>
<p>    Pig iron (saleable)			 +5.0	 +19.2</p>
<p>    Aluminium				     +3.0	  +0.9</p>
<p>    Copper cathodes			     -7.7	  -6.3</p>
<p>    Sugar					   -3.8	  +7.9</p>
<p>    Salt					    +0.0	  +2.2</p>
<p>    Cloth-mill sector			  +14.2	  -3.3</p>
<p>    Cloth-decentralised sector	     +18.4	 +12.5</p>
<p>    Cotton yarn				  +11.5	  +4.5</p>
<p>    Jute manufacture			    +3.2	  -3.5</p>
<p>    Commercial vehicles			+20.2	 +18.6</p>
<p>    Cars					   +20.4	 +19.5</p>
<p>    Jeeps					  +13.6	 +17.2</p>
<p>    Motor cycles				 +27.4	 +23.7</p>
<p>    Auto rickshaws			     +17.2	 +33.4</p>
<p>    Scooter mopeds				+4.3	 +12.8</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>    18 MAJOR INDUSTRIES			 +8.3	  +7.5</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>    OVERALL					 +5.0	  +4.9</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>NOTE - The index includes 24 sectors accounting for 50.4 percent of the overall index of industrial production. The figures are preliminary.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
